CORE
main.c
--apply-loop-contracts _ --no-standard-checks
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
--
The assigns clauses of the inner loops are inferred. Their targets a[i] and
*(p + k) have a non-constant index or offset, so they are widened to
__CPROVER_POINTER_OBJECT(&a[i]) and __CPROVER_POINTER_OBJECT(&p[k]). Like the
targets built from the may-alias information in loop_assigns_inference-05, the
widened targets must carry a source location: the instrumentation of the outer
loop visits the checks generated for the inner loops, and a check without a
source location failed a precondition in instrument_spec_assigns.h.
